#12857
A Smouldering Battlefield~
   The battlefield stretches out in uneasy silence, a broad expanse of churned
mud, shattered wagons, and abandoned siege works. Smoke still coils lazily from
blackened pits and splintered palisades, but no banners fly and no voices
carry. From here, the hilltop forge looms as a dark silhouette against the
night sky, its furnaces the only steady lights in the distance. Below it, a low
fog creeps in from the edges of the field, draping it in a still silence.
~
aci 0 0 12857
E
battefield field around distance out expanse~
   Nightfall has brought silence to the battlefield as each and every soldier
has retreated to their own side to rest and recharge. A light fog makes it
difficult to make out details; you cannot tell which side is winning.
~
E
mud ground grass~
   The ground is mostly mud, divided into a thousand tiny territories by
wagon wheels and lines of bootprints. Only the rare patch of grass offers a
glimmer of green in the sea of brown.
~
E
wagons works shattered~
   Fallen wagons and siege machines line the battlefield, some burned and
others merely smashed.
~
E
smoke~
Smoke rises from parts of the battlefield, joining with the fog.
~
E
up stars sky night~
The endless night sky stretches out above you, twinkling with stars.
~
E
hilltop forge victory silhouette lights~
   Victory Forge sits atop the hill, watching over the silent battlefield like
a sentinel.
~
E
fog~
A low fog hangs in the air.
~
